    <md:title>2.7.4: Writing Consistent and Inconsistent Systems of Equations</md:title>
    <md:uuid>10fbe297-7ece-4081-9cae-59db68ef6370</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<para>Here is an equation: \( 5x-2y=10 \).</para>
<para>Create a second equation that would make a system of equations with:</para>

<!--Q#1-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>One solution</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  
  <para> Compare Your Answer:  </para>
    
    <para>Your answer may vary, but here are some samples. </para>
    
    <para>\(3x - y = 7\)
    \(2x - 5y = 10\)</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Q#2-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>No solutions</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para>Your answer may vary, but here are some samples. </para>
    
    <para>\(5x - 2y = 20\)
      \(5x - 2y = 8\)</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Q#3-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Infinitely many solutions</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para>Your answer may vary, but here are some samples. </para>
    
    <para>\(15x - 6y = 30\)
      \(150x - 20y = 100\)</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
</section>
</content>
